lindon (@VERSION@-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Renamed package from rivolution to lindon (Conflicts:/Replaces:
    against the old rivolution-* packages for a clean upgrade path).
    Debian revision numbering restarts at 1 under the new package
    identity -- "-6" would falsely imply six prior lindon builds when
    none existed before this one.
  * Dropped the "+lindonN" version suffix entirely -- redundant now
    that the package itself is named lindon, and it broke
    rebuild-deb.sh's own revision auto-bump regex, which expects the
    Debian revision digits directly before the closing paren.
  * Internal paths/strings reverted from /usr/share/rivolution/ etc.
    back to vanilla /usr/share/rivendell/ convention; own systemd units
    renamed accordingly (rivolution-stack.target -> rivendell-stack.target,
    rivolution.conf -> rivendell.conf).
  * postinst: fixed database-wipe risk on first rivolution->lindon
    install -- dpkg leaves $OLD_VERSION empty for a Replaces:-triggered
    package-name change, which would otherwise hit the fresh-install
    branch and drop the existing production database. Now also checks
    for a pre-existing /etc/rivendell.d/rd-default.conf before deciding.
  * New: fourth "Action If Previous Event Still Playing" mode across
    rdairplay, rdlogedit and rdlogmanager: "Make Next & Wait max".
    Combines immediate makeNext() (like "Make Next") with a bounded
    safety timeout (like "Wait up to"), avoiding both the too-short
    interstitial problem of plain "Wait up to" on segue-chained clocks
    and the unbounded wait of plain "Make Next". Encoding: GRACE_TIME
    <= -2, timeout_ms = -GRACE_TIME - 2. No database schema change.
  * Fixed a latent side-effect bug in RDLogPlay::transTimerData():
    makeNext() internally calls SetTransTimer(), which can silently
    overwrite the play_trans_line member. The new branch now uses the
    pre-captured local trans_line consistently, matching the existing
    defensive pattern already used elsewhere in the function.
  * Fixed grace-time display bugs: EventWidget::load() (rdlogmanager)
    lost the assignment from event_event->graceTime() during a
    refactor, always showing "Start Immediately" regardless of the
    saved value; RDEventLine::propertiesText() (lib/rdevent_line.cpp)
    didn't know about the new GRACE_TIME <= -2 encoding and rendered
    it as a bogus wrapped-around QTime (e.g. "57:59" for a 2:00
    timeout) in the RDLogManager event list.

 -- RudiOnTheAir <newsletter@schwoon.info>  @DATESTAMP@
